**********************************🚀 Node.js Backend Setup (Simple Notes)*********************************************
1)Create entry file
--server.js or index.js
This is the main starting file
Initialize project

2)Run: npm init -y
It creates: package.json and package-lock.json
Install dependencies
Run: npm install express mysql cors

3)Database connection
Create folder: config
File: db.js
Used to connect Node.js with MySQL database


4)Repository layer
Folder: repositories
File: roles.repository.js
Used to write SQL queries
Direct communication with database


4)Service layer
Folder: services
File: roles.service.js
Used for business logic (validation, processing)
Calls repository


5)Controller layer
Folder: controllers
File: roles.controller.js
Handles request and response
Calls service


6)Router layer
Folder: routes
File: roles.router.js
Used to define API URLs (endpoints)

Example:
router.get('/roles', getRoles);





******************************Correct Architecture *****************************************************************

This is called a layered architecture (or MVC + Service + Repository pattern), not “dependency flow”.

🔄 Request Flow (Top → Bottom)
Client (Frontend / Postman)
index.js (create server)
Router   (define API)
Controller (control req ,res)
Service    (busness logic)
Repository (sql queric those communicate database )
Database


🔄 Response Flow (Bottom → Top)
Database returns data
Repository processes it
Service applies business logic
Controller formats response
Router sends response
Client receives response

controllers/*.js → handle req/res
services/*.js → business logic
repositories/*.js → DB queries
config/db.js → database connection




